<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Himachal Pradesh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Himachal Pradesh is a mountainous state of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalaya</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimla">Shimla</a>. It was created in 1948 as a union of some thirty princely hill states, including Chamba, Mandi and Sirmur, absorbed the hill districts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> in 1966 and became a full state in 1971. It is known for its orchards, hydroelectric power and hill resorts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh.jpg" alt="Himachal Pradesh" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnpetitproleX · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kullu_Valley_near_Manali,_Himachal_Pradesh,_India.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
